{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A refresh action stored in a view’s environment."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"refresh","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RefreshAction","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI13RefreshActionV"},{"text":"? { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"set","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When this environment value contains an instance of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" structure, certain built-in views in the corresponding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" begin offering a refresh capability. They apply the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instance’s handler to any refresh operation that the user initiates.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"By default, the environment value is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":", but you can use the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View\/refreshable(action:)"},{"text":" modifier to create and store a new","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refresh action that uses the handler that you specify:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["List(mailbox.conversations) { conversation in","    ConversationCell(conversation)","}",".refreshable {","    await mailbox.fetch()","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On iOS and iPadOS, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"List"},{"type":"text","text":" in the example above offers a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pull to refresh gesture because it detects the refresh action. When"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the user drags the list down and releases, the list calls the action’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"handler. Because SwiftUI declares the handler as asynchronous, it can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"safely make long-running asynchronous calls, like fetching network data."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Refreshing-Custom-Views","text":"Refreshing Custom Views"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can also offer refresh capability in your custom views."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Read the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh"},{"type":"text","text":" environment value to get the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instance for a given "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment"},{"type":"text","text":". If you find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a non-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" value, change your view’s appearance or behavior to offer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the refresh to the user, and call the instance to conduct the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refresh. You can call the refresh instance directly because it defines"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction\/callAsFunction()"},{"type":"text","text":" method that Swift calls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when you call the instance:"}]},{"code":["struct RefreshableView: View {","    @Environment(\\.refresh) private var refresh","","    var body: some View {","        Button(\"Refresh\") {","            Task {","                await refresh?()","            }","        }","        .disabled(refresh == nil)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Be sure to call the handler asynchronously by preceding it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":". Because the call is asynchronous, you can use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its lifetime to indicate progress to the user. For example,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you can reveal an indeterminate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProgressView"},{"type":"text","text":" before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"calling the handler, and hide it when the handler completes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If your code isn’t already in an asynchronous context, create a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/Swift\/Task","type":"text"},{"text":" for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"method to run in. If you do this, consider adding a way for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"user to cancel the task. For more information, see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Concurrency.html","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Swift Programming Language","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environmentvalues\/refresh"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues\/refresh","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refresh"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI13RefreshActionV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"RefreshAction"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"extendedModule":"OpenSwiftUI","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI17EnvironmentValuesV7refreshAA13RefreshActionVSgvp","title":"refresh","roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property"},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/RefreshAction":{"title":"RefreshAction","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction","role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RefreshAction","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RefreshAction","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/refreshaction","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An action that initiates a refresh operation."}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","title":"OpenSwiftUI","abstract":[],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui","role":"collection"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Environment":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A property wrapper that reads a value from a view’s environment."}],"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environment","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Environment","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Environment","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Environment","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/EnvironmentValues/refresh":{"title":"refresh","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environmentvalues\/refresh","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues\/refresh","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A refresh action stored in a view’s environment."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refresh"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI13RefreshActionV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"RefreshAction"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/EnvironmentValues":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EnvironmentValues","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"EnvironmentValues","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenSwiftUI exposes a collection of values to your app’s views in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"EnvironmentValues","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" structure. To read a value from the structure,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declare a property using the "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" property wrapper and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specify the value’s key path. For example, you can read the current locale:"}],"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environmentvalues","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EnvironmentValues","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues","type":"topic"},"https://docs.swift.org/swift-book/LanguageGuide/Concurrency.html":{"titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Concurrency","type":"text"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Concurrency.html","url":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Concurrency.html","type":"link","title":"Concurrency"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/RefreshAction/callAsFunction()":{"title":"callAsFunction()","abstract":[{"text":"Initiates a refresh action.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/refreshaction\/callasfunction()","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction\/callAsFunction()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"callAsFunction"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}],"type":"topic"}}}